    <mxCell id="key" value="&lt;b&gt;Edges&lt;/b&gt;   1  tracked files are committed and pushed · 2  local .opencode and opencode.json never leave the workstation · 3  the build machine clones tracked content and runs copy-resources · 4  package distributed to consumers · 5  the validator writes the only artefact it is allowed to write · 6  the artefact is attached to the ticket&#10;&lt;b&gt;No runtime service&lt;/b&gt;   this ticket deploys markdown and (optionally) one Node script; there is no server, no container, no database, and therefore no rolling deploy or health endpoint&#10;&lt;b&gt;Consequence for QA&lt;/b&gt;   there is nothing to start. Verification is a file-level scan plus, for OI-09, opening the referenced path in the same tree — see TDD section 10 Runtime Profile" style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#999999;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="430" y="570" width="700" height="95" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
